    <description><![CDATA[<blockquote>
<p><em>&ldquo;I often use “we” in this book to mean you (the reader) and I. It’s a habit I got from my teaching days, as I saw writing as a shared learning experience for both the writer and the readers.&rdquo;</em><br>
— <strong>Huyen Chip</strong></p>
</blockquote>
<hr>
<blockquote>
<p><em>&ldquo;The light is brightest when it is dark.&rdquo;</em><br>
— <strong>Đinh Anh Thi</strong></p>
</blockquote>
<hr>
<blockquote>
<p><em>&ldquo;Remember that, you are a son before becoming a father.&rdquo;</em><br>
— <strong>Đinh Anh Thi</strong></p>
</blockquote>
<hr>
<blockquote>
<p><em>&ldquo;Premature optimization is the root of all evil.&rdquo;</em><br>
— <strong>Donald Knuth</strong></p>]]></description>
